{
  "id": "eyevoice-span",
  "term": "eye–voice span",
  "definition": "Eye–voice span is the time gap between when a person fixates visually on source text and when they begin producing spoken output. In interpreting research, it is used as an indicator of how efficiently visual information is converted into verbal expression, including processes such as word retrieval and sentence planning.",
